## 3.1 Random Seed Generator

The random seed generator produces a seed `r_t` at each generation step.
The seed can depend on the preceding text/context and the watermarking
key.

In the experiments, SynthID-Text uses a sliding-window method in which
the seed is a hash of the most recent `H` tokens together with the
watermarking key.

``` text
H = 4
```

Conceptually:

``` text
r_t = Hash(x_(t-H), ..., x_(t-1), watermarking_key)
```

## 3.2 Sampling Algorithm

The sampling algorithm uses the random seed together with the LLM's
next-token probability distribution.

``` text
Context + Watermark Key
          |
          v
   Random Seed Generator
          |
          v
       Random Seed
          |
          v
 LLM Probability Distribution
          |
          v
    Sampling Algorithm
          |
          v
    Watermarked Token
```

The sampling algorithm introduces a correlation between the generated
token and the random seed. The detector later measures this correlation.

